Here is the commit message:
generated table code fixes

fixed problems

fixed generated table factory method argument ordering

added static access to a table's raw (unnamespaced) table name

uniformed style for generated table code

updated auto generated tables

removed wildcard imports

Here is the root cause:
The generated table factory method (`get<Table>(...)`) produced by the code-generation template was calling `Table.of(t, name, namespace, ...)`, while the actual `of(...)` factory method defined on the generated Table classes expects the parameters in the order `(t, namespace, name, ...)`. This argument-order mismatch meant that whenever a generic (dynamically named) table was constructed via the factory, the `name` and `namespace` values were swapped, causing the table to be built with an incorrect namespace/table name. This is a template-level bug, so every generated Table class inherited the same incorrect calling convention, requiring the generated sources to be regenerated (hence updated `__CLASS_HASH` values, explicit imports, and consistent use of static `Row.of(...)`/`Column.of(...)` factory calls instead of ambiguous bare `of(...)` calls in nested Function/Hydrator classes).

